          "home network manager",
          "Vernet App"
        ],
        "Description": "Take control of your home or office network with Vernet — a free, open-source toolkit that puts network insights in your hands.\n\nWhether you're troubleshooting a slow connection, checking who's on your Wi-Fi, or making sure your devices are reachable, Vernet gives you clear, easy-to-understand answers — no technical background required.\n\n🔍 What's on my network?\nSee every device connected to your local Wi-Fi, along with their IP addresses and names. Know exactly who and what is sharing your connection.\n\n📡 Is my internet working?\nRun a ping test to check if a website or device is responding. Spot drops and delays in seconds.\n\n⚡ How fast is my connection?\nTest your real download and upload speed with the built-in speed test. Get accurate results without leaving the app.\n\n🔓 What services are exposed?\nScan a device for open ports to see which services are reachable — helpful for understanding your home network's security posture.\n\n🌐 What's behind this address?\nUse built-in DNS tools to look up domain names, resolve IPs, and trace how addresses are mapped on the internet.\n\n✅ Free & open source\nVernet is free and open source on GitHub: https://github.com/osociety/vernet\n",
        "Features": [
          "Wifi Details, Find Devices, Device Detail, Open ports scanner, Ping & DNS Lookup, Server Monitoring, IPv4 & IPv6 subnet calculator, Wake on LAN, Switch discovery, Speed test"
        ],
        "ReleaseNotes": "New Support page for donations, stars and ratings.\nChoose whether updates come from GitHub or from the store.\nScan notifications now open the report for that scan.\nWi-Fi signal strength is read correctly on Linux.\nBug fixes and performance improvements.",
